---
// /partners — the CosmOS Certified Technology Program landing page.
//
// Built because the program was named on the homepage but linked from nowhere:
// a developer looking for "the plugin / partner program" had no route to it and
// /partners was a 404 (Philipp Dransfeld, 16 Jun 2026).
//
// Spelling: "Program", not "programme" — matches the registered name
// "CosmOS Certified Technology Program" and the site's US spelling.
//
// Every partner name below is cleared for public use (project context doc, §5,
// Ollie 2026-06-10) and already appears on the homepage logo wall.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Partner program — Sonical"
  description="The CosmOS Certified Technology Program: SDK access, certification and support for developers building audio apps and for the companies building the hardware that runs them."
  canonical="https://www.sonical.ai/partners/"
  eyebrow="Partner program"
  heading='The CosmOS Certified <span class="acc">Technology Program</span>'
  nav="partners"
  centered={true}
>
  <p class="lede">
    One program, three ways in. Build audio apps that run on CosmOS, build the
    devices that run it, or supply the silicon and sensors underneath. Partners
    get SDK access, certification and support.
  </p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>App developers</h3>
        <p>
          Build an audio app once and run it on any CosmOS device, instead of
          porting it to each manufacturer's closed firmware.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>Product makers</h3>
        <p>
          Ship devices that can get better after they leave the factory, using
          Sonical's software and reference designs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rowcard">
        <h3>Technology suppliers</h3>
        <p>
          Put chips, sensors and radios in front of every builder on the
          platform rather than one customer at a time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What partners get</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><b>SDK access.</b> The CosmOS software development kit, with the tools to build and test on-device.</li>
      <li><b>Certification.</b> Verification that what you have built runs correctly on CosmOS devices.</li>
      <li><b>Support.</b> Direct access to the engineering team while you build.</li>
    </ul>
    <!-- TODO: certification criteria, review timeline, and whether there is a
         program fee are not published anywhere. Get these from Larry Golob
         (VP Partnerships & BD, runs the program) before this page claims
         anything more specific. -->
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>How to join</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><b>Tell us what you want to build.</b> Use the form and say which of the three routes fits you. A real person reads every message.</li>
      <li><b>We talk it through.</b> We work out where you fit on the platform and what you would need from us.</li>
      <li><b>You get the SDK and start building.</b> Access is invitation-only for now, so this step follows the conversation rather than a signup.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="ctarow">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/?reason=apps#contact">I build audio apps →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/?reason=products#contact">I make audio products →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/?reason=tech#contact">I supply technology →</a>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Each button opens the contact form on the homepage with your reason already
      ticked. Prefer email? Write to <a href="mailto:info@sonical.ai">info@sonical.ai</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Already on the platform</h2>
    <div class="logo-wall">
      <img src="/logos/fraunhofer.png" alt="Fraunhofer" />
      <img src="/logos/hear360.png" alt="Hear360" />
      <img src="/logos/oikla.png" alt="Oikla" />
      <span class="logo-lockup" role="img" aria-label="Golden Hearing"><img src="/logos/golden-hearing.png" alt="" /><span class="nm"><span>Golden</span><span>Hearing</span></span></span>
      <img src="/logos/hear-angel.png" alt="Hear Angel" />
      <img src="/logos/idun-audio.png" alt="IDUN Audio" />
      <img src="/logos/sigma-connectivity.png" alt="Sigma Connectivity" />
      <img src="/logos/antennaware.png" alt="AntennaWare" />
      <img src="/logos/xmos.png" alt="XMOS" />
      <img src="/logos/renesas.png" alt="Renesas" />
      <img src="/logos/st.png" alt="STMicroelectronics" />
      <img src="/logos/bosch.png" alt="Bosch" />
      <img src="/logos/qorvo.png" alt="Qorvo" />
    </div>
    <p>
      Coverage of what partners are building with us is in the
      <a href="/newsroom/" style="color:var(--text-acc);text-decoration:none">newsroom</a>.
      Remora, the world's first personal hearing computer, has CosmOS inside:
      <a href="https://remora.pro" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--text-acc);text-decoration:none">remora.pro</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Page>
